  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "Since many statistical methods, such as hypothesis testing using regression analysis and analysis of variance, are predicated on the assumption that the data are normally distributed, a standard procedure in most quantitative-genetic investigations is to transform the data to resemble normality as closely as possible prior to analysis. We first consider the logarithmic transform, as it is one of the most common, and successful, normalizing transformations.",
